Leaving my own use case for more context here:

```jsx
function Markdown(props) {
  const { renderedMarkdown, ...other } = props;
  const dangerouslySetInnerHTML =
    typeof renderedMarkdown === "string" ? { __html: renderedMarkdown } : null;

  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={dangerouslySetInnerHTML} {...other} />;
}
```

https://codesandbox.io/s/dangerouslysetinnerhtml-undefined-dhs8i?file=/src/index.js

We're currently migrating from rendering markdown to raw HTML to rendering markdown to JSX (via mdx). The above implementation is a wrapper that makes sure that both approaches are styled the same.

We could just replace the `renderedMarkdown` prop with direct usage of `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
